description:
Зеркало Linear VOS-73: https://linear.app/vostrikov/issue/VOS-73/sdelat-vsplyvayushie-podskazki-na-knopkah-bolee-informativnymi

Пересмотреть tooltip'ы на кнопках UI и заменить короткие/неочевидные подсказки на информативные.

Цель:
- пользователю понятно, что именно сделает кнопка;
- при риске неоднозначности подсказка объясняет результат действия;
- текст короткий, но не телеграфный.

Критерии приемки:
- для основных кнопок интерфейса добавлены/обновлены tooltip'ы;
- подсказки описывают действие в терминах пользователя, а не внутренней реализации;
- одинаковые действия имеют единообразные формулировки.

File: vts/static/app.js:1074-1084.

    const sourceUrl = task.source_url || '';
    ...
    const titleHref = isUpload ? (...) : sourceUrl;
    if (titleHref) { titleEl.href = titleHref; ... }

For non-upload tasks the About-dialog title anchor's href is the raw source_url with no scheme validation. A task created with source_url='javascript:alert(document.cookie)' would produce a clickable title that runs script in the user's own session on click.

Severity: LOW — self-XSS only. source_url is the URL the user themselves submitted to POST /api/tasks (tasks are per-user, not shared), and yt-dlp download would fail on such a URL so the task never completes normally. No cross-user vector.

Root-cause overlap: the same missing validation is the subject of vts-h45 (server-side url scheme allow-list on task creation). Fixing vts-h45 (reject non-http(s) at the API) closes this too; a belt-and-braces client guard (only assign href when /^https?:/i.test(sourceUrl)) is the local fix. Note the codebase already regex-gates the share-intake path (app.js:5120, /https?:\/\//) — same guard, just not applied here.

Confidence: high on the gap, low on exploitability. Batchable/linkable with vts-h45.

Filed by Vector Prime nightly code-review (chunk 4: frontend XSS). For Optimus Prime.
